senses.gloss:
Arcimant (˚mat, ˚ma),
(1) n. of a legendary cakravartin who became the father of Dīpaṃkara: Mv 〔i.193.14〕 ˚māṃ (v.l. ˚mo; n. sg.); 〔198.16〕 ˚mo, etc.;
(2) n. of a previous incarnation of Śākyamuni: LV 〔170.17〕. See also Arciṣmant.

Arciṣmant,
(1) n. of a Tathāgata: Śikṣ 〔9.3〕;
(2) n. of a Bodhisattva: Gv 〔442.11〕;
(3) n. of an ancient king, a previous incarnation of Amitāyus, and father of Puṇyaraśmi: RP 〔36.18 ff.〕 Cf. also Arcimant.
